          ;; V8 defaults to ~984 KiB: recursive guest frames and the\n                 ;; serializers of captured continuations can exhaust it before\n                 ;; Python's 1000-frame guard. 6 MiB fits Linux's 8 MiB native\n                 ;; stack. Re-exec before loading CLJS, covering shadow autorun\n                 ;; AND direct `node ... --test=...` shard invocations.\n                 :prepend \"if (!process.execArgv.includes('--stack-size=6144')) { const child = require('child_process').spawnSync(process.execPath, [...process.execArgv, '--stack-size=6144', ...process.argv.slice(1)], {stdio: 'inherit'}); if (child.error) throw child.error; if (child.signal) process.kill(process.pid, child.signal); else process.exit(child.status); }\"\n                 :autorun true}\n\n          :vm-bench {:target :node-script\n                     :main bench.yin-vm-bench/-main\n                     :output-to \"target/vm-bench.js\"}\n\n          :yin-repl {:target :node-script\n                        :main yin.shell.main/-main\n                        :output-to \"target/yin-repl.js\"}}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793386000000-reviewer-adopt-fix-r2.glm-5.3.findings.md:14:**P2-2 tail-chain stack growth — CLOSED.** Ruling (d): constant stack restored on BOTH lanes. Independent shapes (not the fixture's): 2-arg accumulator self-recursion `(go 1000 0)` → `[:yin.k/ok 1000]`, walker depth 1 at n=0 and n=1000, semantic depth 5 at both — constant; 3-cycle mutual chain (ma→mb→mc→ma, my shape) → `[:yin.k/ok :done]` both lanes, walker 1 / semantic 5, constant 0→1000; sensitivity control: non-tail `(grow n)` semantic depth 5 → 34 (n=10) → 304 (n=100) — the metric grows when it should (walker lane masks depth, as the fixture itself documents). The reinstated assertions (`d100 = d1000`, `≤ d0+2`, both lanes, non-tail negative control) are in `test-outcome-common-call-depth` (clojure_test.clj:1450-1484) and pass in the suite run below. Mechanism: outcome-token fast path in `call-entry`