ect tail application; only published/cross-unit entries take a bridge frame) — and that preserved tail lane is exactly the shape cc3's binding targets. The steward's depth measurements cleared the thresholds (155/155 overlap, max ratio 1.20×, max depth 28 frames; `test/yang/latte_oracle/depth_comparison.md`), so budget work is not at risk. This round proves the **binding** still holds.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794376197000-engineer-cc3-fix-r3.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:119:max path depth 90 / 103,650 path bytes / restated 4,000,000 guest\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793314500000-prior-attempt-context-for-kimi.md:8:**Commit `1eb14d06` — \"fix(yang.clojure): enforce callable admission and restore tail depth\"**\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793314500000-prior-attempt-context-for-kimi.md:13:enforcement, tail-depth restoration, plus ledger rows.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794202500000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.findings.md:53:The recorded branch timeout also occurred **in isolation**, so worker starvation is not an adequate explanation. Cc1 adds occurrence enumeration, correspondence sorting, and origin bookkeeping; these add compilation cost without inherently changing executable tree structure. The PHP prelude-depth defect explains master’s overflow, and `f4df9893` fixes that structure. **That fix is not contained in fa70516f.**\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:294:- `U`: distinct canonical rows; `O`: all occurrence-tree positions; `A`: `:application` occurrences; `D`: maximum path depth; `L`: total encoded length of application paths; separate user, helper, wrapper, prelude, macro-generated and Rule-R counts as derived diagnostic groups.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794513111000-engineer-cc4-fourhost-equality-budget.prompt.md:24:2. **The port landed** (`309fe842` + kit `ba3cc407` + cljd fix `a3f7ab8d`) — yang.clojure's exception lowering is the continuation encoding (`finally` expressible, one-catch pinned; the outcome machinery retired, net −418 lines). Your pinned cohort's expectations must be recorded from POST-port compilation; per the attribution rule above, any budget shift vs the pre-port measurement attributes to the port's Phase 2 (`d60038ef`).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794513111000-engineer-cc4-fourhost-equality-budget.prompt.md:41:   **Attribution (binding at dispatch):** cc4 measures the POST-port lowering (the encoding all four frontends will run — the port merges before cc4 lands). If any budget shifts vs a pre-port measurement, attribute the shift to the port's Phase 2 (`d60038ef`), not a cc4 regression. Measure BOTH: pre-port baseline = the master commit preceding the port's merge; post = the port branch/merged master. The port's Phase 3 depth harness (on its branch) exists for exactly this comparison.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.prompt.md:33:7. **Numeric preflight bounds BEFORE any tagged run** [C: design §6.3 — finite ceilings declared before tagged evidence]: before running the oracle C lanes with binding active, your findings must record the ACTUAL finite numbers: max rows/occurrences/applications/path-depth/path-bytes for the pinned corpus (derive from the compiled fixtures), the trace capacity and byte bound, and the instruction ceilings (the oracle's inspected baseline is 4,000,000 guest instructions and 1,000,000 trace records per C lane — RESTATE them and the occupancy argument for the new binding work; never silently raise fuel). A tagged run before the bounds record exists is a failed round.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793309500000-reviewer-adopt-s1.glm-5.3.findings.md:14:**P2 | test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1355-1384 | Tail-chain stack growth: a documented invariant was dropped, not preserved.** The base asserted `d100 = d1000` (\"depth constant in the iteration count\") and the base comment (clojure.cljc:618-621, rewritten in this diff) guaranteed \"the semantic VM's return stack stays constant through tail chains\". The renamed `test-outcome-common-call-depth` now *asserts* linear growth — 9 frames per source activation (`(= (- d1000 d100) (* 9 (- d100 d0)))`) — and deleted the constant-depth assertion for both lanes. `loop`/`recur` chains remain constant (`test-continuation-depth-gates`, clojure_test.clj:1088). No hard VM depth limit exists (3000-deep named tail recursion completes), but deep named/mutual recursion now consumes ~9 frames/activation, and A2's obligation list includes \"tail behavior\" (fast-path preservation; no fast path exists here). Fix: acceptable only as a recorded architect tradeoff with a follow-up fast path; otherwise the entry/bridge needs a constant-stack design for tail calls.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793386000000-reviewer-adopt-fix-r2.prompt.md:17:- P2-2 tail chains must be constant stack. Ruling: restore constant depth on BOTH lanes; assertions reinstated.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r2.prompt.md:20:2. **The recipe record** (`:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema 1`): closed, versioned; names the interpreter function, the exact reconstruction profile (frontend revision, grammar/options, expansion environment, recorded origins/attempts incl. the Phase 3r rebind mechanics, canonicalization, site-table derivation, lowering rules), input roles, and the oracle's exact schema identity.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794374077000-engineer-cc3-fix-r2.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:142:max path depth 90 / 103,650 path bytes / restated 4,000,000 guest\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795400000000-yangclojure-cc1-findings-and-lane-state-for-reassignment.md:42:The isolated re-run on the branch clone (`847aa885`) FAILED in isolation too — but with DIFFERENT corpus entries failing each time (`:vm-corpus-stack`/`:register`, then `:vm-corpus-semantic` etc.), same \"deadline waiting for response 14\" signature → the deadline is marginal on shiva, not worker starvation and not cc1. The decisive measurement: the SAME test on a CLEAN MASTER clone fails identically — `java.lang.StackOverflowError` on `<?php echo 1 + 2;` across `:vm-corpus-semantic`/`:stack`/`:register`. **RED 2 is a pre-existing master red on shiva**, host-sensitive (a stack depth crossing under shiva's JVM/stack configuration), in the yin.repl shell-session surface. Not worker starvation, not the cc1 branch.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794160000000-engineer-wedge-encoder-layer.prompt.md:30:4. Capture (bounded — no closure serialization): the advanced `:consumer`'s halted/blocked state, continuation depth, and the control node at the top frame at wedge time.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794519755000-engineer-post-port-oracle-reverification.glm-5.3.findings.md:45:**The binding WAS re-derived by the port — in Phase 3r, commit `8456c2e9` (\"port Phase 3r —\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794519755000-engineer-post-port-oracle-reverification.glm-5.3.findings.md:170:- Depth evidence spot-check: `test/yang/latte_oracle/depth_comparison.md` — 155 rows, max ratio\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794519755000-engineer-post-port-oracle-reverification.glm-5.3.findings.md:171:  1.20x (`constructor-mkenv` 5→6), max post-port depth 28 (`check-assume-have-discharge` 32→28) —\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794519755000-engineer-post-port-oracle-reverification.glm-5.3.findings.md:197:Six checklist items: **PASS, PASS, PASS-with-note (rebind, Phase 3r `8456c2e9` — not Phase 4),\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794210000000-engineer-evidence-walk-fix.prompt.md:21:- `kernel-attempt` must not walk the machine: dissoc `:consumer` alongside `:session` from the exception data before `evidence-data` (the machine is diagnostic machinery, same class as the host session — the existing comment at ~:1036 already says so for `:session`). The blocked record keeps `:message`, the causes, and `:host-session-attached?`; add the advanced machine's BOUNDED summary instead if useful (halted/blocked/continuation-depth — scalars only).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793830000000-engineer-h3-1-blocked-fixture-diagnosis.prompt.md:29:3. Bounded snapshots at exhaustion: control position, continuation depth, call frequencies, and the ordered tail of the executed-call/trace stream (bounded — no full dumps).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:27:| Max path depth (flattened steps) | 90 | max over application paths |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
