{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'instruction-provenance|call-sites|defn published' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\ncat shadow-cljs.edn | head -100\nsed -n '345,390p' src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\ncat bin/collab-tools/README.md | rg -n -A35 -B5 rverify\"","aggregated_output":"110:;; through the `publish-module!` result's `:call-sites`, not through\n183:(defn- claims-call-sites?\n200:  (when (claims-call-sites? ast)\n386:            call-sites (when (:rows claim)\n388:                               ;; cc3 item 3: the instruction-provenance\n439:              call-sites (assoc :call-sites call-sites))))))))\n487:(defn published-call-site-table\n494:   `publish-module!` result map (whose `:call-sites :record` and\n509:                                        [:call-sites :record]))\n536:(defn published-instruction-provenance\n551:     (published-instruction-provenance handle\n554:                                               [:call-sites :record]))\n555:     (published-instruction-provenance handle nil record-or-result)))\n634:(defn- mark-call-sites\n642:                           :node (update n field mark-call-sites)\n645:                                            (mapv mark-call-sites children)))\n976:                       :ast (cond-> assembled proven? mark-call-sites)\n;; shadow-cljs configuration\n;; Source paths come from deps.edn (:paths plus the :cljs alias's\n;; :extra-paths); shadow ignores any :source-paths set here when :deps\n;; is used.\n{:deps {:aliases [:cljs]}\n\n :dev-http {9000 \"public\"}\n\n :builds {:demo {:target :browser\n                 :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n                 :modules {:main {:init-fn datomworld.demo/init}}}\n\n          :local {:target :browser\n                  :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n                  :closure-defines {datomworld.demo/WEBSOCKET_PORT 8090}\n                  :modules {:main {:init-fn datomworld.demo/init}}}\n\n          :test {:target :node-test\n                 :output-to \"target/node-tests.js\"\n                 ;; V8 defaults to ~984 KiB: recursive guest frames and the\n                 ;; serializers of captured continuations can exhaust it before\n                 ;; Python's 1000-frame guard. 6 MiB fits Linux's 8 MiB native\n                 ;; stack. Re-exec before loading CLJS, covering shadow autorun\n                 ;; AND direct `node ... --test=...` shard invocations.\n                 :prepend \"if (!process.execArgv.includes('--stack-size=6144')) { const child = require('child_process').spawnSync(process.execPath, [...process.execArgv, '--stack-size=6144', ...process.argv.slice(1)], {stdio: 'inherit'}); if (child.error) throw child.error; if (child.signal) process.kill(process.pid, child.signal); else process.exit(child.status); }\"\n                 :autorun true}\n\n          :vm-bench {:target :node-script\n                     :main bench.yin-vm-bench/-main\n                     :output-to \"target/vm-bench.js\"}\n\n          :yin-repl {:target :node-script\n                        :main yin.shell.main/-main\n                        :output-to \"target/yin-repl.js\"}}}\n   \"yin.vm.ucf.holder.evidence-test\"\n   \"yin.vm.ucf.authority.front-test\"\n   \"yin.vm.ucf.fencing-rows-test\" \"yin.vm.ucf.holder.reader-test\"\n   \"yin.vm.ucf.holder.writer-test\" \"yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver-test\"])\n\n\n;; Read only namespace tokens, never evaluate forms or resolve reader branches.\n;; Include host-only extensions too: existing exclusions name Node/Dart suites.\n(defn check-manifest!\n  \"Check the applicability manifest against a test root; throw with every\n   unlisted namespace (and path) and stale entry before any lane work.\"\n  [test-root included-nses excluded-suites]\n  (let [dirs [\"dao/host\" \"dao/jing\" \"dao/data\" \"dao/space\" \"dao/stream\" \"yin/vm\" \"yin/repl\"]\n        bare [\"dao/jing_test\" \"dao/stream_test\" \"dao/data_test\" \"yin/vm_test\" \"yin/repl_test\"]\n        extensions [\"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljs\" \"cljd\"]\n        files (->> (concat\n                     (mapcat #(->> (fs/glob (fs/path test-root %) \"**\")\n                                   (filter (fn [file]\n                                             (and (fs/regular-file? file)\n                                                  (re-find #\"_test\\.(clj|cljc|cljs|cljd)$\"\n                                                           (str file)))))) dirs)\n                     (for [stem bare ext extensions\n                           :let [file (fs/path test-root (str stem \".\" ext))]\n                           :when (fs/regular-file? file)] file))\n                   (sort-by str))\n        inventory (reduce (fn [acc file]\n                            (if-let [[_ ns-name] (re-find #\"\\(ns\\s+([^\\s()\\[\\]{}\\\";]+)\" (slurp (str file)))]\n                              (update acc ns-name (fnil conj []) (str file))\n                              (throw (ex-info (str \"J2 manifest: no ns form in \" file)\n                                              {:file (str file)}))))\n                          (sorted-map) files)\n        listed (set (concat included-nses (map :ns excluded-suites)))\n        unlisted (remove #(contains? listed %) (keys inventory))\n        stale (sort (remove #(contains? inventory %) listed))]\n    (when (or (seq unlisted) (seq stale))\n      (throw (ex-info\n               (str/join \"\\n\"\n                         (concat [\"J2 manifest FAILED:\"]\n                                 (for [ns-name unlisted]\n                                   (str \"UNLISTED \" ns-name \" -- \"\n                                        (str/join \", \" (get inventory ns-name))))\n                                 (for [ns-name stale]\n                                   (str \"STALE \" ns-name \" -- no test file\"))))\n               {:unlisted (select-keys inventory unlisted) :stale (vec stale)})))\n    {:namespaces (count inventory) :files (count files)}))\n\n12-`plan` with the canonical `--allowed-tools Read \"Bash(git diff *)\" \"Bash(git status *)\"`. A new run needs a\n13-`Session-ID: <uuid>` line in the prompt header (generate and record it first); a resume passes the id as the\n14-last argument. The response goes to `<prompt-stem>.stdout.log`, or the next free `<stem>-r<n>.stdout.log`\n15-if that exists, so no log is ever overwritten. Run it with the harness's background mode; never append `&`.\n16-\n17:## `rverify.sh <host> <scratch-clone> <git-ref> <name> <files-list|-> <cmd>...`\n18-\n19-Applies the uncommitted files named in `<files-list>` (repo-relative paths, one per line, shipped as a tar)\n20-over `<git-ref>` in `~/ci/<scratch-clone>` on `<host>` and runs each command under the mise environment in\n21-tmux session `<name>`. Results land in `~/ci/<name>-logs/` (`rc`, `cmdN.log`, `head`, `DONE`). A setup\n22-failure is written to `rc` as `setup FAILED: ...` and no command runs. The clone is locked while the job runs,\n23-so use one scratch clone per concurrent job; a previous overlay is removed before the next checkout. If a job is killed hard (SIGKILL, reboot) the lock directory `~/ci/<scratch-clone>.lock` is left behind: remove it by hand after checking nothing is running.\n24:`rverify.sh poll <host> <name>` prints `STATE=RUNNING|DONE|NOT-STARTED-OR-DIED` and the `rc` lines.\n25-Host conventions: [`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`](../../docs/agents/build-n-test.md) (\"Remote agent\n26-execution\"); run one Dart lane per host.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
