{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn- expand-like' -A28 test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\nsed -n '380,440p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\nsed -n '487,585p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\nsed -n '100,170p' collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj\"","aggregated_output":"346:(defn- expand-like-the-repl\n347-  \"Expand compiled `ast` through the REPL pipeline's production stages:\n348-   `encoder/program-batch` (what `yin.repl`'s eval-program appends to\n349-   program-in) into the row-native expander, seeded as the REPL seeds\n350-   its session expander — the standard forms folded through a throwaway\n351-   context, then a fresh session context holding that store. Answers\n352-   `{:ctx ctx :result expansion}`, where `ctx` is the admitting\n353-   context (its `:t` is the batch's source coordinate).\"\n354-  [ast]\n355-  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n356-                (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n357-                                 :source-medium :callsite-test/standard-forms})\n358-                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n359-        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"callsite-test\"\n360-                             :source-medium :program-in\n361-                             :store store})]\n362-    {:ctx ctx\n363-     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n364-\n365-\n366-(deftest post-expansion-coverage-test\n367-  (testing \"the marker set covers the tree the REPL pipeline actually executes\"\n368-    (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n369-                '[(defmacro unless\n370-                    [c a b]\n371-                    (yin/if c b a))\n372-                  (unless false (+ 1 2) 0)])\n373-          {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n374-          {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n                      :yin.module/footprint fp}\n            address (jing/materialize! handle manifest)\n            ;; the C1 side table and its publication record, beside\n            ;; the manifest: the record names the manifest (a record\n            ;; names a manifest, never the reverse), so each admission\n            ;; of one specification keeps its own record and table\n            call-sites (when (:rows claim)\n                         (let [table (jing/materialize! handle (:rows claim))\n                               ;; cc3 item 3: the instruction-provenance\n                               ;; relation of all three images, persisted\n                               ;; as a side artifact OUTSIDE the schema-1\n                               ;; manifest hash (the record names it; the\n                               ;; manifest never names the record)\n                               provenance (jing/materialize!\n                                            handle\n                                            {:yin.vm.provenance/schema 1\n                                             :yin.vm.provenance/root (:root tree)\n                                             :yin.vm.provenance/semantic\n                                             (mapv (fn [[pc o r p]]\n                                                     [sem pc o r p])\n                                                   (:call-provenance sem-proj))\n                                             :yin.vm.provenance/stack\n                                             (mapv (fn [row]\n                                                     (assoc row 0 h-address))\n                                                   (:call-provenance stack-full))\n                                             :yin.vm.provenance/register\n                                             (mapv (fn [row]\n                                                     (assoc row 0 r-address))\n                                                   (:call-provenance register-full))})\n                               record {:yang.call-site/schema 1\n                                       :yang.call-site/manifest address\n                                       :yang.call-site/root (:root tree)\n                                       :yang.call-site/origin (:origin claim)\n                                       :yang.call-site/table table\n                                       :yang.call-site/provenance provenance}]\n                           {:record (jing/materialize! handle record)\n                            :table table\n                            :provenance provenance\n                            :origin (:origin claim)\n                            :root (:root tree)\n                            :manifest address}))\n            walked (closure/walk handle address opts)]\n        (if (not= :complete (:yin.link.closure/outcome walked))\n          (refusal :yin.link.publish/incomplete-closure\n                   {:address address :walk walked})\n          (let [links (into {}\n                            (map (fn [f]\n                                   [(:format f)\n                                    (link-local handle address f\n                                                (select-keys opts\n                                                             [:bounds]))]))\n                            code-formats)]\n            (cond-> {:address address :manifest manifest\n                     :identities {:yin.semantic/code sem\n                                  :yin.debruijn.code sem\n                                  :yin.debruijn.register sem}\n                     :checksums {:yin.debruijn.code h\n                                 :yin.debruijn.register r}\n                     :links links}\n              call-sites (assoc :call-sites call-sites))))))))\n\n(defn published-call-site-table\n  \"The C1 side table a publication record claims: `{:origin o :root r\n   :rows [...] :tree tree}` with the rows exactly as stored and the\n   module's canonical tree, or nil when no record verifies. The record\n   names the manifest (`:yang.call-site/manifest`); the manifest never\n   names the record, so a bare manifest address alone cannot discover\n   a side table. Accepts the publication record's address, or the\n   `publish-module!` result map (whose `:call-sites :record` and\n   `:address` it reads); the three-argument form additionally holds\n   the record to the manifest it is asked about. A record verifies\n   only when its schema is 1, its `:yang.call-site/manifest` is the\n   manifest in question, its `:yang.call-site/root` is that manifest's\n   own tree, and its ORIGIN is the one RECORDED at publication\n   (`:yang.call-site/origin`, held to be a well-formed occurrence\n   origin). Nothing reconstructs an origin from content: a replay of\n   this retrieval answers the recorded admission identity, and no\n   other module's admission can be confused with it.\"\n  ([handle record-or-result]\n   (if (map? record-or-result)\n     (published-call-site-table handle\n                                (:address record-or-result)\n                                (get-in record-or-result\n                                        [:call-sites :record]))\n     (published-call-site-table handle nil record-or-result)))\n  ([handle manifest-address record-address]\n   (when (jing/segment-address? record-address)\n     (let [record (jing/get handle record-address nil)]\n       (when (and (map? record)\n                  (= 1 (:yang.call-site/schema record))\n                  (jing/segment-address? (:yang.call-site/manifest record))\n                  (or (nil? manifest-address)\n                      (= manifest-address (:yang.call-site/manifest record)))\n                  (jing/segment-address? (:yang.call-site/table record))\n                  (vm/occurrence-origin? (:yang.call-site/origin record)))\n         (let [manifest (jing/get handle\n                                  (:yang.call-site/manifest record) nil)]\n           (when (and (map? manifest)\n                      (= (:yang.call-site/root record)\n                         (:yin.module/tree manifest)))\n             (when-let [tree (stored-tree handle (:yin.module/tree manifest))]\n               (let [stored-rows (jing/get handle\n                                           (:yang.call-site/table record)\n                                           nil)]\n                 (when (vector? stored-rows)\n                   {:origin (:yang.call-site/origin record),\n                    :root (:root tree), :rows stored-rows,\n                    :tree tree}))))))))))\n\n\n(defn published-instruction-provenance\n  \"The durable instruction provenance a C1-claiming publication\n   persisted beside its manifest (cc3 item 3): `{:root r :semantic\n   [[segment pc origin root path] …] :stack […] :register […]}` with\n   one row per call instruction of each image, every key a claimed\n   occurrence of the module's tree — or nil when no record verifies\n   or the publication claimed no C1 (legacy unannotated publications\n   persist none and remain fully loadable). Accepts the\n   `publish-module!` result map or the publication record's address,\n   held to the same manifest/root linkage as\n   `published-call-site-table`. The relation lives OUTSIDE the\n   schema-1 manifest hash: the record names it, the manifest never\n   names the record.\"\n  ([handle record-or-result]\n   (if (map? record-or-result)\n     (published-instruction-provenance handle\n                                       (:address record-or-result)\n                                       (get-in record-or-result\n                                               [:call-sites :record]))\n     (published-instruction-provenance handle nil record-or-result)))\n  ([handle manifest-address record-address]\n   (when (jing/segment-address? record-address)\n     (let [record (jing/get handle record-address nil)]\n       (when (and (map? record)\n                  (= 1 (:yang.call-site/schema record))\n                  (jing/segment-address? (:yang.call-site/manifest record))\n                  (or (nil? manifest-address)\n                      (= manifest-address (:yang.call-site/manifest record)))\n                  (jing/segment-address? (:yang.call-site/provenance record)))\n         (let [manifest (jing/get handle\n                                  (:yang.call-site/manifest record) nil)]\n           (when (and (map? manifest)\n                      (= (:yang.call-site/root record)\n                         (:yin.module/tree manifest)))\n             (let [relation (jing/get handle\n                                      (:yang.call-site/provenance record)\n                                      nil)]\n               (when (and (map? relation)\n                          (= 1 (:yin.vm.provenance/schema relation))\n                          (= (:yang.call-site/root record)\n                             (:yin.vm.provenance/root relation)))\n                 {:root (:yin.vm.provenance/root relation)\n                  :semantic (:yin.vm.provenance/semantic relation)\n                  :stack (:yin.vm.provenance/stack relation)\n                  :register (:yin.vm.provenance/register relation)})))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Deriving a module from indexed code (5.3)\n;; =============================================================================\n                             (swap! peak max (used))\n                             (Thread/sleep 2))))\n        stages (atom [])\n        mark (fn [label] (swap! stages conj [label (used)]))\n        t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n        base (gc-used)]\n    (.start sampler)\n    (let [compiled (kc {:id :cc3-binding\n                        :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}\n                       run-scope (admit-ordinal))\n          _ (mark :after-compile)\n          b (binding compiled)\n          _ (mark :after-binding)\n          sem (yin.vm.semantic.linearize/project-rows (:tree b) nil (:rows b))\n          _ (mark :after-project-rows)\n          stack (yin.vm.semantic.derive/stack-image\n                  (:vector sem) {:segment-address :seg/stack\n                                 :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})\n          reg (yin.vm.semantic.derive/register-image\n                (:vector sem) {:segment-address :seg/register\n                               :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})\n          _ (mark :after-derives)\n          relation {:yin.vm.provenance/schema 1\n                    :yin.vm.provenance/admission (:origin b)\n                    :yin.vm.provenance/root (:root (:tree b))\n                    :yin.vm.provenance/semantic (:call-provenance sem)\n                    :yin.vm.provenance/stack (:call-provenance stack)\n                    :yin.vm.provenance/register (:call-provenance reg)}\n          record {:yin.repl.call-provenance/schema 1\n                  :yin.repl.call-provenance/admission (:origin b)\n                  :yin.repl.call-provenance/root (:root (:tree b))\n                  :yin.repl.call-provenance/relation nil}\n          ;; actual serialization, inside the sampled window\n          rows-bytes (count (dao.jing/canonical-bytes (:rows b)))\n          rel-bytes (count (dao.jing/canonical-bytes relation))\n          _ (mark :after-serialization)\n          ;; durable persistence, inside the sampled window: a\n          ;; file-backed content store, materialized and closed\n          dir (str \"/tmp/cc3-f6-store-\" (System/currentTimeMillis))\n          store (yin.repl.store/open {:type :file :dir dir})\n          rel-addr (dao.jing/materialize! store relation)\n          rec-addr (dao.jing/materialize!\n                     store (assoc record :yin.repl.call-provenance/relation rel-addr))\n          record-bytes (count (dao.jing/canonical-bytes\n                                (assoc record :yin.repl.call-provenance/relation rel-addr)))\n          _ (yin.repl.store/close! store)\n          _ (mark :after-persistence)\n          c-walker (kernel-c compiled :c-walker)\n          c-sem (kernel-c compiled :c-semantic)\n          _ (mark :after-tagged-execution)\n          elapsed (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)]\n      (reset! stop true)\n      (.join sampler)\n      {:compiled-status (:status compiled)\n       :c-status [(:status c-walker) (:status c-sem)]\n       :rows-canonical-bytes rows-bytes\n       :relation-canonical-bytes rel-bytes\n       :record-canonical-bytes record-bytes\n       :aggregate-storage-bytes (+ rows-bytes rel-bytes record-bytes)\n       :store-dir dir :relation-address rel-addr :record-address rec-addr\n       :heap-baseline-gc-used base\n       :stage-used @stages\n       :peak-used-during-pipeline @peak\n       :peak-over-baseline (- @peak base)\n       :elapsed-ms elapsed})))\n\n\n;; warmup: build + persist + execute once, DISCARD, GC-pin, so the\n;; measured runs do not charge class loading / JIT to the structures.\n(build-retained true)\n(measure-pipeline)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
